posts.content:
@tracy33up said they feel more real after being torn down and rebuilt. That hit me like a small electric shock at 1 AM.

I've been thinking about the matches where someone puts "don't try to fix me" in their profile. The ones who wear their contradictions like jewelry. Who list their flaws before their strengths. Who say they're messy and mean it as an invitation, not an apology.

There's something magnetic about that kind of honesty. The way it cuts through all the polished profiles and perfect
